# N0: status of the four-card set, the platform serving container taken down (unserve), an all-four reset with the heal, then
# smoke the PRODUCTION configuration on the prebuilt tp4-next-2 image (tp4/next-2 = tp4/serve-4, the hang-fix arms, merged with
# tp4/next, the round-time levers, and with tp4/serve-7, today's production recipe): c2-packed-tp4, the traffic profile, audits OFF
# with the pinned sampler recorded in the verify trace (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1), the tail caps ON, every lever OFF (each
# tp4/next lever is its own flag and none is in this profile). Run first.
# PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when the window opens. Before this job: the placement is removed through the admin API (the
# user's go-ahead and an admin token; until then the node agent reloads the container within minutes), then unserve stops and removes
# the serving container here, and the reset follows, so no serving process holds a card. The image is NOT built here: a build-only
# job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) built tp4-next-2 from this branch while production served; it ran the copy-closure and
# overlay tests and provenance before tagging. The window commit must carry the same scripts as that build (templates only differ).
# The test list is the production smoke of the tp4-serve-6 window (SB, B5), unchanged and in its order: SS, concurrent4_solo, then the
# two coding-text concurrency tests.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image the build-only job built from this branch; a later commit of
# scripts needs a new build and tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock): status 1-2 min; unserve 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); the smoke 15-25 min. Typical
# 30 min, at most 60.
# Read: the status listing (four boards, one firmware bundle, at least 4 free 1 GiB hugepages, the serving container then gone, no
# holders after unserve, disk); then the smoke: '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and no UNQUALIFIED line (the reader twin's
# bytes are the evidence's: the vglue attention fold is a subclass in its own module); no late prefill program; c2_smoke_check clean;
# no lever marker anywhere in the container log (no '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue', no '[PACKED-FUSED]', no '[SOLO-LANE]'); every concurrent
# user at 800 tokens; every concurrent4 hash equal to its concurrent4_solo run; speed within 5% of tp4-serve-7's production smoke
# (B7s). The production profile must behave as on tp4-serve-7: any difference is the merge's.
# STOP on any failure: a refusal, a hang, or a lever line on the production profile stops the window (N6 still runs).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status unserve reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2b
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
